# Round glm2card's decode card, a rewrite of round glmlift's (its terms predate glmswap, glmgemm2, glmpp3, glmnext,
# glmtiles and the S4 body): GLM-5.3-Flash at the serving defaults (the NextN MTP draft, residency mid-p0-s1) on
# plan (a), the A6000 alone, against plan (b′) (--place bp: plan (a) with the 3090 an expert tier under the host
# tier), one binary, decode at prose depth 512, n 96, ctx 2048, one stream. With docs/cards/glmbp-pp.card (pp512,
# read from the same log) it decides whether the GLM seat's unset --place moves from a to bp.
# Decomposition [derived], one drafted pass: two rows one layer apart on one stream (crates/gpu-glm5next/src/pair.rs
# :1-9), the host serving one row's leg while the card runs the other row's layer, so the pass is the sum over the
# layers of max(host legs, card work) (V4.1's pair measured 2H, 09-24, specs multiseq2 msstagger):
# - placement: the 3090 holds 1,501 experts, 38..39 a layer on the 39 card-routable layers (3..10, 13..43; 11, 12
#   and 44 carry Q6_K downs and stay host-only, glm5next/place.rs card_routed): its 24,176 MiB less the context 512,
#   scratch 64, margin 1,024, the tier batch reserve 80.7 MiB (placement/workstation.rs:443) and the reserve plan_rule
#   takes off every card, the tier's Fill included (placement.rs:1792-1801): plan_nextn_slots' NextN bytes, arena
#   16 MiB, prompt front 144.7 MB, card tiles 153.2 MB, two group units 134.4 MB (glm5next/place.rs:789-791). The
#   same formulas less the last three give 1,532; glmlift's seat --plan read 1,531. The tier ids follow the stage
#   card's prefix; the A6000 keeps ~2,568, 65..66 a layer (glmnext's 2,593 plain at ctx 4352, +3 at 2048, -18 the
#   NextN bytes, -10 the second KDA lane), the same in both arms.
# - host slots a row, replayed over the ik router set glm5next-prose (tools/ref/router-residency.py's replay, the tier
#   ids `away`; 24 contexts, 512 prompt ids kept 0, then 96 positions in passes of two rows, both kept at alpha
#   0.829; the mid rule, 1 spare, live 2 passes on; its plain-step arm gives glmres-ab's 39.5 % hit and 212.8 slots):
#   plan (a) 206.0 on the 39 layers + 24 on the Q6_K layers, stage hit 34.0 %; bp 166.9 + 24, stage hit 32.7 %, tier
#   13.8 % of the slots (13.4 % for uniform routing): -39.1 a row (37.3..41.3 over the contexts), -17 %.
# - host leg: 0.111..0.117 ms a slot (glmres-ab.card), the second row 0.93..1.0 of its own (glmpair-probe.card), F
#   2.5..3.5 ms a row: 1.25..1.40 ms a layer-pair on (a), 1.03..1.17 on bp; the host leg -8.4..-9.1 ms a pass.
# - A6000 a layer-pair: 2 x (front 0.23..0.34 ms, latent layers x1.0..1.3 + the shared expert 0.045 + 2.6..2.7 card
#   slots at 0.025..0.035): 0.70..1.10 ms. The front is C1 = S1 47.7 - h 29.6..31.4 - F (glmpair-probe.card) less
#   the dense layers and the head, over 42 layers. In the host's shadow on (a) (0..5 layers card-bound); 0..27
#   card-bound layers on bp, where the card caps the tier's slots.
# - c_two (V4.1's bp steps sit 1.9..2.5 ms over its plan (a) calibration, docs/plan-triage.md:355, rig-log
#   09-29#chatlist-dspark; source open): card-side a tiered row-layer (0.050..0.066 ms, in the card term above, hidden
#   where the host leads), or once a pass (1.9..2.5 ms on the wall). Not both: one term fit V4.1's rows.
# - the 3090: ~1.1 tier slots a row-layer, ~0.04..0.06 ms, inside the row's 0.47..0.58 ms host leg. PCIe a row-layer:
#   16 KB of activation to the 3090, ~18 KB of rows back, read by the A6000's join through the mapping: ~2.7 MB a pass
#   on each link, under 0.1 ms at 26.28 GB/s (docs/facts.md:66). Host DRAM: nothing new (~4 MB a pass).
# - unchanged: the Q6_K layers (6.0..6.5 ms a pass), the dense lead and heads (3..5), the NextN walk (2.4..2.7,
#   layer 45 host-only), the commit (0.3..1.0), the residency's landing waits (0..12 ms a pass,
#   glmresmtp-stage.card's 8..51 ms a landing).
# Pass (a) 60.6..82.1 ms, bp 52.2..76.3 ms; plan (a) 22.3..30.2 tok/s at alpha 0.829. Effect over the grid of every
# term above: +4.7..+16.3 %, median +11.7, written outward as +4.5..+16.5. The edge nearest 0 is the front at
# 0.34 ms, latent layers x1.3 and c_two card-side. A front of 0.37 (h at the 147.7 GB/s peak, not the measured
# slot rate) would put that edge at +2.5 %.
# Acceptance: the tier runs its ids (n_l..n_l+t_l, about 66..104) on card kernels where (a) runs them on the host,
# and the residency picks other flips, so the greedy streams may part and each arm keeps its own positions a
# pass, the same every round: a bias, not a scatter. The band is a pass-time effect: the verdict reads the tok/s
# ratio over the arms' positions/pass ratio and reports both.
# Sitting: one runner invocation serves both cards (its bp/a pair prints `ratio place d=512` and
# `ratio place pp p=512`); lease_take checks one card, this one, so glmbp-pp.card is checked with card.py check
# before the sitting and read from the same log. From the tree that holds both cards in docs/cards:
#   BLOOMERY_AB_ROUNDS=4 BLOOMERY_BOX_ENV='BLOOMERY_TIMING_CARDS=a6000+3090
#   BLOOMERY_LEASE_CARD=docs/cards/glmbp-ab.card' just depth-gpu-glm5next
#   oursmtp:512@BLOOMERY_RESIDENCY=mid-p0-s1,place=a oursmtp:512@BLOOMERY_RESIDENCY=mid-p0-s1,place=bp > <log> 2>&1
# Wall [derived]: 2 arms x (4 rounds + 1 warm-up) = 10 processes at 1.1..2.1 min (a load at 45..75 s, the glmnext
# and glmlane2 cards; the bp load uploads ~22.8 GB more; each arm's preheat, which after a bp arm re-reads the
# ~63 GB its load dropped; 512 prompt ids, 96 generated): 12..22 min; at 3 rounds 10..18.
kind: ab
question: on the serving defaults (NextN draft + residency mid-p0-s1), does plan (b′), the 3090 as GLM's expert
  tier, decode faster than plan (a) on the A6000 alone, by the host slots the tier takes less what the A6000 and
  the two-card cost hand back?
term: pass-time effect @ n=96, depth 512, A6000+3090 (the 3090 idle under a), prose ids (GLM_PROSE from
  GLM_PROSE_FROM), ctx 2048, BLOOMERY_DRAFT=mtp BLOOMERY_RESIDENCY=mid-p0-s1, --place bp against --place a, same
  binary, paired by round: the runner's `ratio place d=512` (bp / a, tok/s) over the arms' mtp positions/pass
  ratio (bp / a), less 1
unit: %
predict: +4.5..+16.5
rounds: 4
sd: 0.6 % AGENTS.md 「Know the ruler」, same-binary paired ratio SD
condition: one runner invocation, both arms in one lease (BLOOMERY_TIMING_CARDS=a6000+3090), every row's card
  field A6000+3090, each witness block naming both cards with the 3090 at its 250 W cap and no Xid before or after
  any arm; a fresh process a run, each starting at the residency seed; every ok row carries the residency column
  `residency mid-p0-s1 (set)` and its `mtp positions/pass` (the runner fails a row without either); the runner's
  cards check holds the bp arm's load record to the A6000 then the 3090 and the a arm's to the A6000 alone; on the
  rows' plan columns card_experts is the same within 1 (2,550..2,590) and host_experts(a) - host_experts(bp), the
  tier's count, reads 1,490..1,515 (another count rescales the tier's term on paper, 39.1 slots a row x count /
  1,501, and needs no re-sit); no row carries [cold], [cpu-busy] or [other-busy]; the full output to a file first
decide-in: two cards decode faster: move the GLM seat's unset --place from a to bp
  (crates/gpu-gates/src/bin/shared/serve_seats/glm.rs, README, docs/BUILD.md) only when this reading's lower bound
  is above 0 and glmbp-pp.card's reading of the same log has its lower bound above 0 too (one --place default,
  flipped only when two cards are not slower, user 2026-10-02); else keep a and act on that card's decision; then
  sit both rows in the A6000+3090 table and open tier-slot residency as the next decode lever
decide-below: below +4.5 the A6000's per-layer work caps the tier's slots more than the band's front allows, or
  c_two sits once a pass above 2.5 ms: with the lower bound still above 0 the default may move as in decide-in,
  with the pp card; at or below 0 keep --place a whatever the pp card reads; either way one nsys window of the bp
  pair pass (host legs, the A6000's per-layer work, the tier's go and count words) before any tier lever
decide-above: above +16.5 move the default as in decide-in, with the pp card; (a)'s host legs or landing waits run
  longer than the band holds (bp's shorter legs open the staging window more): one functional run of each arm
  under generate_glm5next for the residency pass records' wait_us (the runner keeps none on an ok row) before
  pricing the staging-window lever (crates/gpu/src/host/swap.rs:815)
